    {
      "id": "g56y76s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.2 Horticulture"
    },
    {
      "id": "dvlbcrn",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "ds4r5yb",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Himachal_Pradesh_CONSTABLE/images/image_ds4r5yb.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "HP is India's leading apple-producing state, contributing about 25–30% of national apple production. Horticulture has transformed HP's economy, particularly in Shimla, Kullu, Kinnaur, and Mandi districts.",
      "id": "7sbhdpk"
    },
    {
      "id": "y0skn6k",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Dr. Samuel Stokes (Satyanand Stokes): American missionary who introduced apples to Thanedar (Shimla) in 1916; known as 'Apple Man of HP/India'.",
        "A.J. Oakley: Also credited with introducing the 'Delicious' variety at Kotgarh (Shimla) around the same period.",
        "The apple economy generates thousands of crores of rupees annually for HP farmers.",
        "Other fruits: Pear (Mandi, Kullu), Plum (Kullu, Shimla), Cherry (Shimla, Kullu), Apricot (Kinnaur, Lahaul), Peach (Kullu), Walnut (Kinnaur), Almond (Kinnaur, Lahaul).",
        "Stone fruits (apricot, cherry, plum) – important in Lahaul and Kinnaur.",
        "Kinnow and citrus fruits: Una, Hamirpur, lower Kangra.",
        "Hops (for beer): Grown in Kullu and Lahaul; supplied to breweries.",
        "Floriculture: Rose, marigold, lily, chrysanthemum grown for commercial markets.",
        "HPMC (HP Horticulture Produce Marketing and Processing Corporation): Markets and processes fruits.",
        "Mushroom cultivation: Solan is known as 'Mushroom City of India'.",
        "HP Controlled Atmosphere (CA) stores: For storing apples off-season; govt-supported."
      ]
    },
    {
